Me wrote:

>is there any reason to use the tune to open the castle, vs just
>busting the drawbridge down with a wand of striking?

Absolutely.  Because once you know the passtune you can use the
drawbridge as a weapon in its own right.

Lower the bridge.  Monsters come storming across.
Play the tune. Raise the bridge.  Monster on bridge goes into the moat.
If it isn't amphibious or flying, it's dead.   Monster on space right
of bridge gets smashed by the portcullis into strawberry jam.  If it
isn't a Xorn or earth elemental, it's dead as well.

Lower the bridge again.   More monsters come across.  Raise the bridge.
Smash them too. Rinse and repeat as necessary.

I use this tactic to dispose of liches, disenchanters and suchlike I
don't want to get close to.  It's also a good way to get rid of a troll
forever.  I also get an evil cackle out of doing it :).

The disadvantage is that you'll lose any objects the creature was
carrying.  But it's a useful option to be able to simultaneously kill
whatever-it-is AND give yourself a breather until you're ready to lower
the bridge again.  

